  "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and all tests pass. Here's what I fixed:\n\n**Root cause**: The `withoutCode` function was defined but never used in `extractMentions` or `highlightMentions`, causing mentions inside code blocks to be extracted and trigger notifications.\n\n**Changes made**:\n\n1. **`extractMentions`** (line 27): Now calls `withoutCode(body)` to strip code blocks before extracting mentions. This prevents mentions inside code blocks from being identified for notifications.\n\n2. **`highlightMentions`** (lines 68-97): Implemented a more sophisticated approach that:\n   - Temporarily replaces code blocks (both fenced ``` and inline `) with unique placeholders\n   - Applies mention highlighting only to the body without code blocks  \n   - Restores the original code blocks\n\nThis ensures mentions inside code blocks are neither extracted for notifications nor highlighted in the display.",
